        {
          "id": 3379182349,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The issue was found while testing a candidate WSLua feature (get_capture_file_info()), where the new entry point is reachable from a Lua tap draw() callback after sequential close on a pipe capture\n\nSo are there cases where some code really needs to know how large the file is when 1) it's a pipe and 2) it's been closed?",
